                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Whispers of a Machine is a nice, mellow point-and-click detective game.  I played through 3 times to try the different \"personality\" paths and had a good time.  You get different augments depending on your personality which changes how you deal with some situations.  There are some puzzles but it's mostly what thing to click or what item to use.  It's usually not hard to figure out.\n\n✅Easy controls (mostly mouse), no timers/time limits, 3 different ways to play, no bugs/issues.\n😐Short-ish at 6 hours, but you can play more than once to try other things.\n❌Would have liked a windowed option.\n\nI had a good time.  Nothing stressful about it.  It took me (who is pretty slow) about 6 hours for a playthrough, which sounds short, but it fits the story.  It's easy to recommend this game to others.",
